build-line 2026-10-18 · a mutation on loopback is no longer authorised by having arrived on loopback: every page the operator visits can POST to 127.0.0.1, and `/api/limb` reaches shell and python, so POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE now need the token on loopback too (the portal is handed it at load; local scripts read data/token, 0600) while reads stay open so the health bar keeps working · a Host header that is not this machine is refused on a loopback-bound console (DNS rebinding), unless LYGO_TRUSTED_PROXY says a reverse proxy rewrites it · a turn whose context contains fetched web text no longer auto-dispatches shell/python_exec/rust_exec/cargo: the call is recorded as REFUSED with the reason, because otherwise whoever wrote the page chooses what runs here; LYGO_WEB_TAINT_EXEC=1 is the documented opt-out · the upload control sends the token it now needs
